      en: "Bottrop is situated on the Emscher River, a central waterway in the Ruhr region. The city lies on the gentle slopes of the Ruhr basin, with elevations between 30 and 100 meters above sea level. The landscape is shaped by spoil tips from mining, such as the Halde Beckstraße, which rises 80 meters above the surrounding area. Bottrop has several lakes formed by mining subsidence, like the Heidesee. The climate is maritime temperate, with average January temperatures near 2°C and July around 18°C. The Emscher River is being renaturalized as part of the Emschergenossenschaft project. Green corridors connect the city to the Hohe Mark Nature Park and the Kirchheller Heide forest.",
